{
  "_note": "Common mistakes (/grammatica/errori-comuni): Italian words learners mix up and expressions they build wrongly. Each pair has two sides (a, b: the word, its part of speech or a note in English, an Italian example with <b>), `why` the difference in one sentence, `tr` its translation into the help languages (empty for now: the page shows nothing then), `check` a gap to try (`answer` = a or b; `options` when the words on the buttons are not the bare a/b words). `regel` per group is the folding rule (*…* = example, **…** = bold), `regelTr` its translation, `comic` the comic at the top (MascotComic). `wrong: true` on b = this isn't correct Italian, and its `ex` is an English note, not an example. Meaning traps (false friends) are on /conoscenze/falsi-amici, not here. The part-of-speech cards on /grammatica/parti-del-discorso point to a pair here through `fehler`. Standard Italian; variety it-IT on every pair. Group ids stay: the styles use them. idioms-mistakes run (2026-11-14), not yet reviewed.",
